Do not dereference a failed TIFF open in xdvipsk's LoadTIFF().

Open() returns NULL when libtiff rejects the file (for example a TIFF
truncated before its directory), and LoadTIFF() read fio->tif from it
unconditionally, so such an image crashed xdvipsk with SIGSEGV; the
build with the bundled libtiff crashed the same way. Throw into the
existing catch block instead, so em:graph reports "Unable to read file".

Not Gentoo-specific; applies after the system-libtiff patch.

diff --git a/texk/xdvipsk/graphlib/loadTIFF.cpp b/texk/xdvipsk/graphlib/loadTIFF.cpp
index bf5f031..a4f24a4 100644
--- a/texk/xdvipsk/graphlib/loadTIFF.cpp
+++ b/texk/xdvipsk/graphlib/loadTIFF.cpp
@@ -730,6 +730,10 @@ LoadTIFF(BitmapIO *io, fi_handle handle, int page, int flags) {
 
 	try {	
 		data = Open(io, handle, TRUE);
+		if (!data) {
+			// Open() has already reported that libtiff rejected the file.
+			throw (char*)NULL;
+		}
 		fi_TIFFIO *fio = (fi_TIFFIO*)data;
 		tif = fio->tif;
 
